 Open the moderator area using the hostname your audience can reach. On a quiz page, **Start a game** opens a new big screen. Participants can scan the QR code or enter its URL and join by name. **Start** opens the first active question. Use **Finish** to reveal the votes and the correct choices, then **Next** (or **End quiz**). Returning to the join link on the same browser resumes that player's game.
 
+To time each question, set **Timer minutes** and **Timer seconds** in quiz settings before starting the game. Leave both at 0 for manual timing. Only the big screen shows the countdown. At zero, the answers are revealed just as if you clicked **Finish**; you can still finish early. Reloading does not restart the clock. Timer settings are not exported.
+
 Each run has its own join code, players and answers. The big screen and phones update in place; the QR code, JavaScript, and fonts are served locally. See [implementation notes](docs/implementation.md) for reconnect and presence behavior.
 
