diff --git a/docs/implementation.md b/docs/implementation.md
index eb4faf6..e6807a0 100644
--- a/docs/implementation.md
+++ b/docs/implementation.md
@@ -15,6 +15,12 @@
 
 **Presence vs. participation.** Presence is a renewable lease per open tab; the denominator counts distinct players with a current lease. A departure beacon or a closed socket removes a tab. If neither arrives, two missed heartbeats (55 seconds) age it out. Player identities and submitted votes survive all of these. The numerator and per-option reveal totals count saved answers, even from a phone that has since left.
 
+## Question timer
+
+Each game snapshots the quiz duration in seconds. Opening a timed round sets `games.closes_at` from the same server timestamp as `game_rounds.opened_at`; closing clears it. Only the projector gets the remaining time, which it animates locally between server updates. An untimed game has no deadline or scheduled job.
+
+After commit, Active Job schedules an in-process wake-up for that game and round. The server boot hook restores outstanding wake-ups from SQLite. Live requests also reconcile overdue rounds, and the vote transaction checks the deadline before accepting a pick. The job and manual Finish use the same version-checked transition, so neither pending jobs nor stale forms can close the next round or score twice. No worker service or browser needs to stay connected for a timer to expire.
+
 ## Scoring and prizes
 
 - The prize count is snapshotted with the quiz content when the game is created. Old exports that omit `number_of_winners` still import with the default of 3. Non-default counts round-trip; live results are never exported.
